---Runtime configuration for the organization. Response for GetRuntimeConfig.
---@class gcp.apigee_v1.GoogleCloudApigeeV1RuntimeConfig
---@field traceBucket? string Cloud Storage bucket used for uploading Trace records.
---@field analyticsBucket? string Cloud Storage bucket used for uploading Analytics records.
---@field name? string Name of the resource in the following format: `organizations/{org}/runtimeConfig`.
---@field tenantProjectId? string Output only. Tenant project ID associated with the Apigee organization. The tenant project is used to host Google-managed resources that are dedicated to this Apigee organization. Clients have limited access to resources within the tenant project used to support Apigee runtime instances. Access to the tenant project is managed using SetSyncAuthorization. It can be empty if the tenant project hasn't been created yet.

---Runtime configuration for the Spec Generation add-on. All fields are proto3 primitives (bool, string, double) rather than google.protobuf.*Value wrappers because the runtime consumer deserializes the JSON via Gson field reflection with no registered type adapters. Wrapper types would serialize as JSON objects/null that Gson cannot bind to Java primitive fields.
---@class gcp.apigee_v1.GoogleCloudApigeeV1RuntimeSpecGenerationAddonConfig
---@field samplingRate? number Fraction of eligible transactions to capture, in [0.0, 1.0]. The consumer enforces an internal upper-bound clamp independently of this field. Default: 0.0 (omitted from JSON per proto3 default-scalar-omission; the consumer's field initializer supplies the effective 0.01 fallback).
---@field enabled? boolean Whether the Spec Generation add-on is active for this environment. Default: false.
---@field rawObservationsPubsubTopic? string Full Pub/Sub topic path in the Apigee Runtime Tenant Project where the message processor publishes captured RawObservation messages. Format: projects/{project}/topics/{topic}. Empty string is the "not configured" sentinel; the consumer short-circuits publishing when empty. Default: empty string.
---@field apiObservationsPubsubTopic? string Full Pub/Sub topic path in the Apigee Runtime Tenant Project where the Schema Inferring Engine publishes inferred ApiObservation messages. Format: projects/{project}/topics/{topic}. Same sentinel semantics as raw_observations_pubsub_topic. Default: empty string.
---@field enabledUntil? string ISO-8601 timestamp until which Spec Generation remains active (e.g. "2026-12-31T23:59:59Z"). Empty string is the canonical "not configured" sentinel and MUST be treated by the consumer as "expired" (short-circuit before parsing). Default: empty string.

---NEXT ID: 13 RuntimeTraceConfig defines the configurations for distributed trace in an environment.
---@class gcp.apigee_v1.GoogleCloudApigeeV1RuntimeTraceConfig
---@field revisionCreateTime? string The timestamp that the revision was created or updated.
---@field endpoint? string Endpoint of the exporter.
---@field otelCollectorSecurityScheme? gcp.apigee_v1.GoogleCloudApigeeV1RuntimeTraceConfigOtelCollectorSecuritySchemeEnum Optional. Security scheme for the outbound connection to the customer-owned OpenTelemetry Collector. Only meaningful when `exporter` is `OPEN_TELEMETRY_COLLECTOR`. Runtime consumers unaware of a value should treat it as `OTEL_COLLECTOR_SECURITY_SCHEME_UNSPECIFIED` (== NONE).
---@field spanSemantics? gcp.apigee_v1.GoogleCloudApigeeV1RuntimeTraceConfigSpanSemanticsEnum Optional. The span semantics to use. Configuration Requirements (if `span_semantics` is `OTEL`): - `trace_protocol` must be `OTLP`.
---@field overrides? gcp.apigee_v1.GoogleCloudApigeeV1RuntimeTraceConfigOverrideList List of trace configuration overrides for spicific API proxies.
---@field exporter? gcp.apigee_v1.GoogleCloudApigeeV1RuntimeTraceConfigExporterEnum Exporter that is used to view the distributed trace captured using OpenCensus. An exporter sends traces to any backend that is capable of consuming them. Recorded spans can be exported by registered exporters.
---@field mTlsConfig? gcp.apigee_v1.GoogleCloudApigeeV1RuntimeTraceConfigOtelMtlsConfig Optional. mTLS configuration for the OTel Collector endpoint. Required when `otel_collector_security_scheme` is `MTLS`; must be absent otherwise.
---@field samplingConfig? gcp.apigee_v1.GoogleCloudApigeeV1RuntimeTraceSamplingConfig Trace configuration for all API proxies in an environment.
---@field name? string Name of the trace config in the following format: `organizations/{org}/environment/{env}/traceConfig`
---@field openTelemetryProtocolEnabled? boolean Optional. If `true`, the runtime uses OpenTelemetry Protocol (OTLP) to send trace data. Configuration Requirements (if `open_telemetry_protocol_enabled` is `true`): - Allowed `Exporter`s: `CLOUD_TRACE` or `OPEN_TELEMETRY_COLLECTOR`. - If `Exporter` is `OPEN_TELEMETRY_COLLECTOR`: - `endpoint` refers to a valid OTLP collector URL. - If `Exporter` is `CLOUD_TRACE`: - `endpoint` refers to a valid project ID Deprecated: Use trace_protocol instead.
---@field traceProtocol? gcp.apigee_v1.GoogleCloudApigeeV1RuntimeTraceConfigTraceProtocolEnum Optional. The trace protocol to use.
---@field revisionId? string Revision number which can be used by the runtime to detect if the trace config has changed between two versions.

---@alias gcp.apigee_v1.GoogleCloudApigeeV1RuntimeTraceConfigExporterEnum "EXPORTER_UNSPECIFIED"|"JAEGER"|"CLOUD_TRACE"|"OPEN_TELEMETRY_COLLECTOR"|"OPEN_TELEMETRY_CLOUD_TRACE"

---@alias gcp.apigee_v1.GoogleCloudApigeeV1RuntimeTraceConfigOtelCollectorSecuritySchemeEnum "OTEL_COLLECTOR_SECURITY_SCHEME_UNSPECIFIED"|"NONE"|"MTLS"

---Runtime-side view of `TraceConfig.OtelMtlsConfig` for the outbound OTel Collector mTLS connection. Shape mirrors `TlsInfoConfig` (in this same file, above) exactly. The oneof discriminates between a direct keystore reference and a `ref://`-indirected reference; both are surfaced on the wire without flattening. The referenced keystore must also appear in `EnvironmentConfig.keystores[]` so the underlying alias bytes are available at runtime. Referential integrity is enforced at trace-config update time: any PATCH that references a keystore not already present is rejected in the same transaction that would persist the update, and keystore/alias/reference deletion is blocked while a trace-config references it.
---@class gcp.apigee_v1.GoogleCloudApigeeV1RuntimeTraceConfigOtelMtlsConfig
---@field keyAliasReference? gcp.apigee_v1.GoogleCloudApigeeV1KeyAliasReference Reference name and alias-id pair. Set when the customer supplied a `ref://{referenceID}` URI in `TraceConfig.OtelMtlsConfig.key_store`. Resolved via the References catalog the same way as `TlsInfoConfig.key_alias_reference` in target-server TLS. Reuses the top-level `KeyAliasReference` message defined for `TlsInfoConfig` above; no new message.
---@field keyAlias? string Full alias resource name of the client-side key/cert alias. Format: `organizations/{org}/environments/{env}/keystores/{keystore}/aliases/{alias}` Set when the customer supplied a plain keystore ID in `TraceConfig.OtelMtlsConfig.key_store`.
---@field trustStore? string Full resource name of the truststore holding the CA(s) that signed the OTel Collector's server certificate. Either a keystore or a reference resource name, mirroring `TlsInfoConfig.trust_store` above: `organizations/{org}/environments/{env}/keystores/{keystore}` `organizations/{org}/environments/{env}/references/{reference}`

