---@field revenueShareType? gcp.apigee_v1.GoogleCloudApigeeV1RatePlanRevenueShareTypeEnum|string Method used to calculate the revenue that is shared with developers.
---@field displayName? string Display name of the rate plan.
---@field description? string Description of the rate plan.
---@field endTime? string Time when the rate plan will expire in milliseconds since epoch. Set to 0 or `null` to indicate that the rate plan should never expire.
---@field setupFee? gcp.apigee_v1.GoogleTypeMoney Initial, one-time fee paid when purchasing the API product.
---@field consumptionPricingRates? gcp.apigee_v1.GoogleCloudApigeeV1RateRangeList API call volume ranges and the fees charged when the total number of API calls is within a given range. The method used to calculate the final fee depends on the selected pricing model. For example, if the pricing model is `BANDED` and the ranges are defined as follows: ``` { "start": 1, "end": 100, "fee": 2 }, { "start": 101, "end": 200, "fee": 1.50 }, { "start": 201, "end": 0, "fee": 1 }, } ``` Then the following fees would be charged based on the total number of API calls (assuming the currency selected is `USD`): * 50 calls cost 50 x $2 = $100 * 150 calls cost 100 x $2 + 50 x $1.5 = $275 * 250 calls cost 100 x $2 + 100 x $1.5 + 50 x $1 = $400 * 500 calls cost 100 x $2 + 100 x $1.5 + 300 x $1 = $650
---@field revenueShareRates? gcp.apigee_v1.GoogleCloudApigeeV1RevenueShareRangeList Details of the revenue sharing model.
